#!/bin/sh
case "$#:$1" in
  '1:--all') busybox --list; printf '\nAdditional programs: nano curl lua joe ed links\nPortfolio helpers: help welcome open browse reboot commands games\nGames: tetris 2048 and /opt/nbsdgames/bin/* (games opens its menu)\n'; exit 0 ;;
  '0:'|'1:--help') ;;
  *) printf 'Usage: commands [--all]\n' >&2; exit 1 ;;
esac
cat <<'TOOLS'
Tools by task
=============

Files        ls cd pwd tree find cp mv rm mkdir ln chmod
Reading      cat less head tail
Searching    grep sort uniq wc cut sed awk
Editing      nano vi joe ed
Archives     tar gzip gunzip unzip
Processes    ps top kill sleep
System       uname hostname id date uptime free df du
Programming  sh lua
Games        games nbsdgames tetris 2048 mines sudoku battleship snakeduel
Network      curl ping wget links (internet access is disabled)

Portfolio    help welcome open browse reboot

Use COMMAND --help for options. cd is built into the shell.
games opens the New BSD Games menu; help games lists controls and sources.
commands --all lists every BusyBox applet.
TOOLS
